WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:18.943
Jonathan nearly bumped into Marissa on his way to the school cafeteria on Monday.

2
00:00:18.944 --> 00:00:26.577
He flashed her a smile, but Marissa's eyes narrowed before she quickly looked away and rushed past him.

3
00:00:26.578 --> 00:00:30.827
Jonathan knew he had to do something about her. And about her father.

4
00:00:30.828 --> 00:00:34.744
He needed to grow a backbone—a very large backbone.

5
00:00:34.745 --> 00:00:43.070
He was so distracted at lunchtime, he dipped his French fries in milk instead of ketchup, and he bit into his orange before remembering to peel it.

6
00:00:43.071 --> 00:00:49.491
Later he got out his history textbook in science class and accidentally went to his English classroom when it was time for math.

7
00:00:49.492 --> 00:00:52.563
It took him forever to do his homework after school.

8
00:00:52.564 --> 00:00:58.134
Whenever he looked at his books, all he saw were soccer balls and Marissa's pretty face.

9
00:00:58.135 --> 00:01:01.260
During dinner that night, Jonathan's mother frowned.

10
00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:06.318
"You love meatloaf, but you've hardly touched it tonight. What's the matter, Johnnyboy?"

11
00:01:06.318 --> 00:01:11.633
"Please don't call me that, Mom. I'm not a baby anymore," Jonathan said.

12
00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:15.775
"I'll try not to," Mrs. Cho promised. "But tell me what's wrong."

13
00:01:15.776 --> 00:01:19.126
Jonathan speared his meatloaf with his fork.

14
00:01:19.126 --> 00:01:22.646
"I wish I were on a different soccer team," he muttered.

15
00:01:22.647 --> 00:01:25.114
Mr. Cho nodded his agreement.

16
00:01:25.115 --> 00:01:30.043
"I wish you were too. I don't like how your coach is running things," he said.

17
00:01:30.044 --> 00:01:35.031
"I'll call him tomorrow and tell him to give you and the other boys more chances with the ball."

18
00:01:35.032 --> 00:01:41.283
"Good idea," Jonathan's mother said. "I'll talk to him too and ask him to stop yelling at the team."

19
00:01:41.284 --> 00:01:46.526
Pastrami yapped in support. Or maybe he just wanted food.

20
00:01:46.527 --> 00:01:51.953
Jonathan slipped Pastrami some meatloaf under the table.

21
00:01:51.953 --> 00:01:57.426
He thought about his parents' offers to speak to his coach. That would make things easy for him.

22
00:01:57.427 --> 00:02:02.091
But how could he complain about his parents babying him if he let them speak on his behalf?

23
00:02:02.092 --> 00:02:06.414
Jonathan looked up and shook his head. "Thanks for offering to help.

24
00:02:06.415 --> 00:02:10.848
I appreciate it. But I want to handle things myself."

25
00:02:10.849 --> 00:02:17.330
His mother peered closely at him. "That's fine, Jonathan. But how?" she asked.

26
00:02:17.331 --> 00:02:23.257
Jonathan shrugged. He wasn't exactly sure what he would do. But he had to do something.

27
00:02:23.258 --> 00:02:28.412
"Well, we'll back you up," his dad said. "You can always count on us."

28
00:02:28.413 --> 00:02:30.741
"Thanks," Jonathan said.

29
00:02:30.742 --> 00:02:35.984
Mrs. Cho grinned. "But only if you stop feeding Pastrami under the table!"

30
00:02:35.984 --> 00:02:40.983
Jonathan grinned back. His parents were pretty smart sometimes!

31
00:02:40.984 --> 00:02:48.140
By the next day, Jonathan had a plan. After school he walked to the park across the street.

32
00:02:48.141 --> 00:02:59.804
He found Max there, just as he'd expected, kicking a soccer ball against a wall with his left foot and then his right and then his left, over and over.

33
00:02:59.805 --> 00:03:02.780
Practicing soccer alone seemed really boring.

34
00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:05.633
"Can I talk to you?" Jonathan asked.

35
00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:11.622
Max trapped the ball under one foot and turned toward Jonathan. "Sure. What's up?"

36
00:03:11.622 --> 00:03:17.359
"I want to apologize," Jonathan said. "I've been blaming you for things that your dad does.

37
00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.590
It's not your fault that he makes everyone give you the ball."

38
00:03:20.591 --> 00:03:25.590
He grinned. "Just like it's not my fault that my mom calls me Johnnyboy."

39
00:03:25.591 --> 00:03:32.933
Max smiled too. "Thank you for that. My dad is very demanding, but at least he doesn't call me a dumb name."

40
00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:39.100
"Whoa!" Jonathan said. He made his eyes bulge out and dropped his jaw as far as it could go.

41
00:03:39.101 --> 00:03:42.782
"Why are you making that crazy face?" Max asked.

42
00:03:42.783 --> 00:03:48.557
"Because I'm in shock from witnessing a miracle: Max Wattenbarger actually smiled."

43
00:03:48.558 --> 00:03:56.325
Max smiled wider. "I should do that more often—it feels good. I know I take soccer too seriously sometimes."

44
00:03:56.326 --> 00:04:05.259
He hesitated for a second. "And I need to apologize to you too. I should have asked my dad to give everyone on the team a chance with the ball.

45
00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.567
I didn't want to hurt his feelings or make him mad.

46
00:04:08.568 --> 00:04:12.908
He's so proud of me, and he works really hard to make me a better soccer player.

47
00:04:12.909 --> 00:04:18.392
Plus, honestly, I couldn't get up the nerve to ask him. He'd get furious at me."

48
00:04:18.393 --> 00:04:24.808
"I should have asked him too," Jonathan said. "I didn't have the nerve either. I get it."

49
00:04:24.809 --> 00:04:32.227
"Good, but can you get this?" Max ran off with the ball, dribbling it through the park.

50
00:04:32.228 --> 00:04:41.549
Jonathan chased after him, but Max was too fast. Suddenly Carlos ran over and stole the ball from Max.

51
00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.883
"Nice going," Jonathan said. "When did you get here?"

52
00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:48.701
"Just now," Carlos replied.

53
00:04:48.702 --> 00:04:54.455
"I spotted someone dribbling a soccer ball faster than the speed of light, and I knew it had to be Max."

54
00:04:54.456 --> 00:04:59.194
"Don't exaggerate," Jonathan said. "Max doesn't run that fast.

55
00:04:59.195 --> 00:05:03.273
Though he can probably beat most cars, trains, and airplanes."

56
00:05:03.274 --> 00:05:06.598
Max laughed.

57
00:05:06.599 --> 00:05:15.114
Jonathan pretended to faint. He said, "Max, you set two huge records today. You smiled and you laughed."

58
00:05:15.115 --> 00:05:19.029
Soon all three boys were laughing.

59
00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:27.517
Then they kicked the ball around and practiced the double fake and hip fake moves that Max had taught them the week before.

60
00:05:27.517 --> 00:05:31.096
When they got tired, they sat on the grass.

61
00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:36.343
"A few weeks ago, I only wanted to win soccer games," Carlos said.

62
00:05:36.344 --> 00:05:42.842
"But it's no fun to win soccer if you hardly ever get the ball. I'd rather lose and have fun."

63
00:05:42.843 --> 00:05:45.616
"Me too," Jonathan agreed.

64
00:05:45.617 --> 00:05:47.669
Max nodded glumly.

65
00:05:47.669 --> 00:05:52.581
"My dad means well, but having me hog the ball isn't fair to the rest of the team."

66
00:05:52.582 --> 00:05:59.153
Carlos started laughing. "At one point Jonathan was so mad at you, he was scheming ways to get rid of you.

67
00:05:59.154 --> 00:06:03.637
He wanted to infect you with cold germs so you'd get too sick to play!"

68
00:06:03.638 --> 00:06:08.497
Jonathan instantly felt bad. "I wasn't serious about that!"

69
00:06:08.498 --> 00:06:13.065
Max shrugged. "It's cool. We're friends now."

70
00:06:13.065 --> 00:06:16.049
"How about a group hug?" Jonathan joked.

71
00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.469
Carlos pretended to throw up.

72
00:06:18.469 --> 00:06:21.656
"How about a fist bump instead?" Max asked.

73
00:06:21.658 --> 00:06:26.687
Jonathan nodded and held up his fist.

74
00:06:26.687 --> 00:06:32.140
On the way home later, Jonathan thought about how a lot of people had been changing their minds lately.

75
00:06:32.141 --> 00:06:35.291
His parents had changed their minds about contacting the coach.

76
00:06:35.292 --> 00:06:39.119
Carlos had changed his mind about winning soccer at all costs.

77
00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:44.952
And Jonathan had changed his own mind about Max. Max was actually a pretty nice kid.

78
00:06:44.953 --> 00:06:50.860
"So maybe," Jonathan thought, "it's possible for Marissa to change her mind about me."

79
00:06:50.861 --> 00:07:00.528
He just had to figure out a way to make that happen.
